e down there do we think it's too  early to tell there was an announcement  of a hundred day plan a plan to make a  plan for improved relations over the  next hundred days and we'll see if that  yields anything there wasn't any  announcement of any meaningful progress  on trade on South China Sea on on North  Korea but maybe the  is the beginning of an improved  relationship but it's too early to trump  said it was outstanding relation well  everything is outstanding for him the  question is is there a strategy to  change the situation with all of these  issues and right now yes it's easy to  have a press conference it's easy to  tweet it's even easy to shoot missiles  but to have a comprehensive strategy  that's going to change real things in  the world that's actually hard and we  haven't seen that I wonder how  disconcerted the Chinese are about this  president's bluster on trade thus far  because president Trump's withdrawal  from the trans-pacific partnership has  greatly benefited the Chinese Li you  must actually be sort of happy with  where things are at right the Chinese  are thrilled because right there was  certainly a level of nervousness with  President Trump coming in and all the  tough talk and then there's really been  no meaningful action to date and not  only that a president Trump has removed  as you correctly say I t's removed the  leverage that we've spent a decade  building and so from a Chinese  perspective the United States has is  coming from a much weaker position China  has been massively strengthened and yes  we can fire some missiles but the  question is is there a strategy and  president Trump doesn't even have a  foreign policy team so how could you  have a real strategy without the people  to develop that strategy well the  president has accepted the Chinese  president's invitation to visit we'll  see what happens when he goes could be  interesting maybe mental thank you very  much
 

